  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Image Assets**\n\nI\'m currently focused on evaluating those generated images, specifically `/src/assets/images/hero_pitch_boot_1794307152243.jpg` and `/src/assets/images/product_carbon_boot_1794307152493.jpg`, looking at their aspect ratios and impressive detail. The others are also worth investigating. I\'m taking notes.\n\n\n**Expanding Image Assessment**\n\nI\'ve expanded my image analysis to include four more assets: `product_match_jersey`, `product_match_ball`, `product_leather_boot`, and `product_gk_gloves`. They all share a 4:3 aspect ratio, just like the others. I\'m taking notes on potential implications for layout and design. I am also reviewing the rules from `frontend-design`, particularly those related to the top bar. I am paying close attention to the single-row, three-zone contract and the specific elements within each zone.\n\n\n**Refining Typography Strategy**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into typography. I\'ve decided to load Google Fonts, focusing on a 2+1 font rule. I\'m thinking of using Barlow Condensed and Outfit for display/brand headings, Plus Jakarta Sans for body prose, and JetBrains Mono for tabular data. I am adhering to a strict type scale for hero headlines, ensuring a balanced text wrap and no unnecessary all-caps or ghost text. I am also planning on keeping metadata clean and unboxed inline, avoiding rounded pill boxes.\n\n\n**Defining Interactive Elements**\n\nI\'m now thinking specifically about how text is presented, including typographic separators like `\302\267` and `/`. I am also focused on interactive filter controls, specifically ensuring that they function as `<button>` elements with click handlers within a clear segmented bar. Also, I am going to limit each card to one subtle unboxed text tag like `Limited Run` or `FIFA Quality Pro`, avoiding badge-like layouts.\n\n**Structuring Layout Precisely**\n\nI am now focusing on the layout\'s structure, with a maximum of four storefront sections. Section one will be the hero section. I\'m planning a two-column split with `items-stretch`. The left column has an editorial campaign story, ground condition spec, and a route to the collection plus customizer. The right has a `16:9` / full-height floodlit carbon boot showcase and interactive technical callout hotspot switch. Below that is a full-width 4-column technical proof strip.\n\n\n**Outlining Site Sections**\n\nI\'m now detailing sections two, three, and four. Section two focuses on a featured collection grid. I\'m imagining interactive elements like search inputs, category filters, and a pitch surface recommender, alongside a product grid. Section three will be a personalization studio where users can customize jerseys and boots. Section four will be a quiet editorial footer.\n\n\n**Defining Purchase Funnel**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in the contiguous purchase module, considering both PDP modal/drawer and the slide-over cart/checkout. I\'m focusing on the user experience; I\'ve designed a clear journey from product selection through to purchase completion. This includes the implementation of a sticky gallery and a corresponding purchase module. I\'ve designed the module with a UK/EU/US size converter and stud configuration selector (`FG / SG / AG`). I\'ve also incorporated a squad number/ID personalization option and stock availability indicators, along with a size guide toggle and an \"Add to Match Bag\" call to action. I\'ve also created a **Match Bag & Checkout Drawer** which will display the itemized list. This will include custom personalization details and a quantity stepper. I\'m also going to have a free express courier threshold progress bar. In addition, I will create payment options and an interactive post-order confirmation and live order tracker.\n\n\n"
